        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Compute a timeout from the nearest timer (0 if ready queue non-empty)",
            "Poll the selector, blocking up to that timeout",
            "Move due timers + I/O callbacks into the ==ready queue==",
            "Run **everything** in the queue, then repeat"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()",
            "fut = loop.create_future()",
            "loop.call_soon(fut.set_result, 7)",
            "v = await fut  # Task parks here",
            "print(v)       # 7, next iteration"
          ],
          "note": "get_event_loop() here is deprecated"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Task Drives the Coroutine",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A coroutine runs **only** once a ==Task== wraps it",
            "Task is a ==Future subclass== that steps the coroutine from a callback",
            "`await fut`: the Task suspends and stays off the ready queue",
            "When `fut` completes, it runs `call_soon(task.__step)`, and the Task resumes"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
