      "page_title": "Future States & How await Parks",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is a Future",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==Future== = a placeholder for a result not ready yet",
            "Three states: {blue:pending} → {red:cancelled} or {green:finished}",
            "Create with `loop.create_future()`, **not** `asyncio.Future()`",
            "Why: alternative loops like ==uvloop== supply a faster Future"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "State",
            "done()",
            "cancelled()",
            "result()"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "{blue:pending}",
              "False",
              "False",
              "InvalidStateError"
            ],
            [
              "{red:cancelled}",
              "True",
              "True",
              "CancelledError"
            ],
            [
              "{green:finished} (value)",
              "True",
              "False",
              "__returns v__"
            ],
            [
              "{green:finished} (exc)",
              "True",
              "False",
              "**re-raises** exc"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Finish It Once",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "fut = loop.create_future()",
            "fut.set_result(42)   # finished",
            "# or: fut.set_exception(err)",
            "fut.set_result(1)  # InvalidState",
            "fut.cancel()         # False",
            "fut.done(), fut.cancelled() # T,F"
          ],
          "note": "second set_* raises InvalidStateError"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`set_result(v)` / `set_exception(e)` move it to ==finished==",
            "`cancel(msg=None)` returns **False** if already done",
            "`done()` = finished or cancelled; `cancelled()` = cancelled only"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. How await Parks a Task",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "await fut",
                "sub": "in coroutine",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "__await__",
                "sub": "yields fut",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "Task parks",
                "sub": "not rescheduled",
                "ink": "orange"
              },
              {
                "text": "set_result(v)",
                "sub": "fut completes",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "Task resumes",
                "sub": "await returns v",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A Future is ==awaitable==: `__await__` yields the Future itself",
            "The Task sees it and **waits**; it is not stepped again",
            "Completion schedules the next step (callbacks: see p.3)"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "def on_done(x):",
            "    if not fut.done():  # guard",
            "        fut.set_result(x)",
            "await asyncio.wait_for(fut, 5)"
          ],
          "note": "timeout may cancel fut first"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. asyncio vs concurrent Future",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Aspect",
            "asyncio.Future",
            "concurrent.futures"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Thread-safe",
              "**No**",
              "Yes"
            ],
            [
              "Wait with",
              "`await fut`",
              "`.result()` blocks"
            ],
            [
              "Bound to",
              "its creating loop",
              "any thread"
            ],
            [
              "Convert",
              "← `wrap_future(cf)`",
              "source"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "the awaitable placeholder"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Bridging, Converting & Cancelling Futures",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "text": "Create the future inside the running loop, finish it exactly once, and always read its result or exception."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Example: Bridge a Callback",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def fetch(api):",
            "  fut = loop.create_future()",
            "  api.start(on_done=fut.set_result)",
            "  return await fut  # parks here"
          ],
          "note": "callback API becomes awaitable"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`asyncio.Future()` directly → skips the loop's own implementation",
            "Late callback, no `done()` guard → **InvalidStateError**",
            "Exception never read → =='Future exception was never retrieved'== at GC",
            "Await a Future from another loop → **RuntimeError**",
            "`set_result` from a worker thread → use call_soon_threadsafe (p.4)"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Converting Futures",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "cf = pool.submit(work)  # thread",
            "af = asyncio.wrap_future(cf)",
            "v = await af   # loop-friendly"
          ],
          "note": "bridges concurrent → asyncio"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`asyncio.Future` is **not** thread-safe: loop thread only",
            "`concurrent.futures.Future` blocks on `.result()`",
            "`run_in_executor` already calls ==wrap_future== for you"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Always Retrieve Errors",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "fut.set_exception(ValueError())",
            "del fut   # never awaited",
            "# GC logs: Future exception",
            "#   was never retrieved"
          ],
          "note": "await it or call fut.exception()"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "9. Cancel with a Message",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "fut.cancel(msg=\"shutdown\") # True",
            "fut.cancel()   # False, done",
            "try: fut.result()",
            "except CancelledError as e:",
            "    print(e.args)  # ('shutdown',)"
          ],
          "note": "msg travels with CancelledError"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "cancel() on",
            "Returns",
            "done() after"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "{blue:pending}",
              "**True**",
              "True"
            ],
            [
              "{green:finished}",
              "False",
              "True"
            ],
            [
              "{red:cancelled}",
              "False",
              "True"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Loop-bound",
          "text": "A Future belongs to the loop that made it. Create it with `get_running_loop().create_future()` in the coroutine that awaits it."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "the awaitable placeholder"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Done Callbacks & call_soon Ordering",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What a done callback is",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==add_done_callback(cb)== calls `cb(fut)` once the Future completes",
            "cb receives the **Future**, not the result: call `fut.result()`",
            "Only arg is the Future (plus `context=`) → extra args via `functools.partial`",
            "`remove_done_callback(cb)` drops **every** registration of cb, returns the count"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "def on_done(fut):",
            "    print(fut.result())",
            "fut.add_done_callback(on_done)",
            "fut.add_done_callback(",
            "    partial(log, \"job-7\"))",
            "# log(\"job-7\", fut)"
          ],
          "note": "cb(fut), never cb(result)"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Never inline: call_soon",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`set_result` **schedules** each callback with `loop.call_soon`",
            "They run on a __later__ loop iteration, not inside set_result",
            "Future already done? New callback **still** goes via call_soon",
            "`call_soon(cb, *args)` appends to the ==ready queue==: FIFO order"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Call",
            "Returns",
            "Runs"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`call_soon(cb, *a)`",
              "Handle",
              "next iteration"
            ],
            [
              "`call_later(d, cb)`",
              "TimerHandle",
              "now + d"
            ],
            [
              "`call_at(t, cb)`",
              "TimerHandle",
              "when time() ≥ t"
            ],
            [
              "`h.cancel()`",
              "None",
              "**never**"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "now = loop.time()  # monotonic",
            "h = loop.call_at(now + 5, ping)",
            "# same as call_later(5, ping)",
            "h.cancel()   # ping never runs"
          ],
          "note": "loop.time(), not time.time()"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Timers use the loop's ==monotonic clock==, `loop.time()`",
            "Each callback runs in a `contextvars.Context` **copy** (`context=`)",
            "A ContextVar set before scheduling is visible inside cb"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Example: who prints first",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "loop.call_soon(print, \"A\")",
            "fut.add_done_callback(",
            "    lambda f: print(\"C\"))",
            "fut.set_result(1)  # queues C",
            "print(\"B\")         # runs now",
            "# output: B, A, C"
          ],
          "note": "set_result returns before C runs"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Catch slow callbacks",
          "text": "`asyncio.run(main(), debug=True)` warns about any callback slower than ==slow_callback_duration== (100 ms): \"Executing <Handle …> took 0.250 seconds\". Thread-safe scheduling is covered on page 4."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "done callbacks, call_soon"
    },
