        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Common mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Expecting cb to run **inside** `set_result`: it runs later",
            "`add_done_callback(cb, x)`: TypeError, wrap with `partial`",
            "Raise in cb? Loop survives: goes to `call_exception_handler`, logged",
            "Slow cb **blocks the whole loop**: no task or I/O runs"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Handles & Timers",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "h = loop.call_later(30, expire)",
            "if got_reply:",
            "    h.cancel()  # timer dropped",
            "h.cancelled()   # True"
          ],
          "note": "keep the handle to cancel it"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Exception Handler",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "def on_err(loop, ctx):",
            "    log(ctx[\"message\"],",
            "        ctx.get(\"exception\"))",
            "loop.set_exception_handler(on_err)"
          ],
          "note": "callback errors land here, not raised"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Keep callbacks **short**: offload blocking work to `to_thread`",
            "Check `fut.cancelled()` before `fut.result()` in cb",
            "Use `partial`, not lambdas capturing loop variables",
            "Run tests with ==debug mode== on"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "done callbacks, call_soon"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "call_soon_threadsafe, the Self-Pipe & Signals",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Comparison",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "call_soon",
            "call_soon_threadsafe"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Caller",
              "loop's **own** thread",
              "**any** thread"
            ],
            [
              "Wakes loop?",
              "no",
              "yes, ==self-pipe=="
            ],
            [
              "Cost",
              "cheaper",
              "+ 1 pipe write"
            ],
            [
              "Use in",
              "callbacks, coroutines",
              "workers, signals"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`call_soon` only appends to the ==ready queue==, with no lock",
            "It assumes the **loop's thread** is the caller",
            "Called from another thread, it can **race** on the queue",
            "A loop asleep in `select()` won't wake, so the callback stalls"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Mechanism: self-pipe",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "worker thread",
                "sub": "call_soon_threadsafe(cb)",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "append cb",
                "sub": "to _ready",
                "ink": "black"
              },
              {
                "text": "_write_to_self()",
                "sub": "1 byte → self-pipe",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              {
                "text": "select() returns",
                "sub": "pipe is readable",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "cb runs",
                "sub": "on loop thread",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Debug mode catches it",
          "items": [
            "`PYTHONASYNCIODEBUG=1` or `asyncio.run(main(), debug=True)`",
            "Non-threadsafe loop method called from the wrong thread → **RuntimeError**",
            "Leave it on in tests to find hidden races"
          ],
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Example: crossing threads",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "def worker(loop, fut):",
            "    v = compute()   # blocking",
            "    loop.call_soon_threadsafe(",
            "        fut.set_result, v)"
          ],
          "note": "never fut.set_result(v) from here"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Direction",
            "API",
