      "page_title": "Protocol Callbacks & Stream Framing",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What Is It"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A ==transport== owns the socket and does the I/O: **how** bytes move. A ==protocol== holds your logic: **what** to do with the bytes.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Transports and protocols come in __pairs__: one of each per connection",
            "The {blue:loop} builds the transport, not your code",
            "The loop calls protocol methods as events arrive",
            "The protocol talks back only through `self.transport`"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Protocol Callbacks"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "class Echo(asyncio.Protocol):",
            "  def connection_made(self, t):",
            "    self.t = t     # keep it",
            "  def data_received(self, d):",
            "    self.t.write(d)  # echo back",
            "  def connection_lost(self, e):"
          ],
          "note": "loop calls these, you never do"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Callback",
            "When",
            "Note"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`connection_made(t)`",
              "first, once",
              "save transport"
            ],
            [
              "`data_received(d)`",
              "0+ times",
              "raw chunk"
            ],
            [
              "`eof_received()`",
              "peer sent EOF",
              "truthy → ==half-open=="
            ],
            [
              "`connection_lost(exc)`",
              "**exactly once**",
              "None = clean"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "connection_made",
                "sub": "once",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "data_received*",
                "sub": "0..n",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "eof_received?",
                "sub": "optional",
                "ink": "orange"
              },
              {
                "text": "connection_lost",
                "sub": "exactly once",
                "ink": "red"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Order is **guaranteed**; nothing arrives after `connection_lost`",
            "`connection_lost(None)` → clean close",
            "`connection_lost(exc)` → the error that broke the link",
            "`eof_received` returns truthy → you can still write",
            "Returns `None`/`False` → transport closes itself"
          ],
          "style": "check"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Framing the Byte Stream"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "def data_received(self, data):",
            "  self.buf += data  # accumulate",
            "  while b\"\\n\" in self.buf:",
            "    line, _, self.buf = \\",
            "      self.buf.partition(b\"\\n\")",
            "    self.handle(line)"
          ],
          "note": "chunks ≠ messages: always buffer"
        }
      ],
